MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_001: Alright, then. Please get these to Ribeira village.\nIt's not urgent, so just whenever's convenient.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_002: Hey, Peter! Doing some shopping?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_003: Yeah, I figured I'd send some toys to my younger\nbrothers back home.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_004: What a nice thing to do. So you're a big brother?\nI've got a little brother and a little sister.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_005: They team up on me with all the "big sister" requests,\nso they can be a bit of a handful.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_006: Oh, believe me—I get it. At home, my brothers pile\nonto me.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_007: Hmhm. Tialla's an only child, and so's Cai. So you're\nthe only one I can talk to about this, Peter.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_008: Cai said he's an only child? Well, I guess that's true,\nbut still...
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_009: Me and Cai are basically foster brothers. My mom\nwas his wet nurse.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_010: Huh. Yeah, I knew you were close. You do seem like\nreal brothers.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_011: And your mother must be very kind to take such\ngood care of a baby that wasn't hers.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_012: Mom and Castor knew each other from a long time\nago, I guess.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_013: She said he showed up, fell to the ground, and\nbegged her to save his child.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_014: That's surprising. I've always thought of Castor as\nthis tough, intimidating guy.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_015: Really? He's a strong, friendly, good person.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_016: Windstorm Castor is famous in the temples. You\nshould hear Centurio talk about him.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_017: Once there was this knight whose attitude he didn't\nlike. He sent him flying right out the temple doors!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_018: Also, according to temple records, he once stood fast\nagainst 50 intruders, spilling a sea of their blood.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_019: Is that all true? I guess Castor was pretty scary\nback then.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_020: There was a point when he mellowed out. Judging by\nthe timing, it had a lot to do with Aurora.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_021: Wow, you really have the inside scoop. I bet you\nknow everything about the temples.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_022: I've browsed through all the temple records.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_023: What I've read covers everything since the founding\nof Aurora's temple about 850 years ago, give or take.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_024: You read all that?! Ultand, that's amazing! I've got to\nhear more of your temple stories.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_C_025: Hmhmhm, OK! But let's keep it between us. And you\nhave to tell me about yourself too.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_001: Hold this down, fasten that, then...
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_002: Yah! Aww... Failed again.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_003: What's the matter, Peter? You're making some funny\nnoises over here.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_004: Oh, wow. That's an old doll. And it's in bad shape.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_005: Yeah, it's Tialla's doll. It means a lot to her, and I\nbroke it.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_006: I've been doing my best to fix it, but...it's not going\nvery well.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_007: Well, shove over, and let me offer some sisterly help!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_008: Really?! That'd be great.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_009: So I made Tialla mad...because I'm hopeless.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_010: I'm sure everything will be OK. I know you two can\npatch things up.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_011: Alright! I secured this part here, so now we just need\nto reinforce it, and it'll be fine.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_012: Thank you so much! I think I've got it from here.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_013: You're good at this, and your fingers are so nimble.\nYou've really got it all figured out, Ultand. 
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_014: That's not true at all. You should see me at home.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_015: My little brother and sister get so mad at me for\nalways forgetting to chop the firewood.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_016: Mom's always yelling at me too. "Get your lazy bones\nout of bed! Go outside! Move your butt!"
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_017: That's how they did things at the temple of Aurora\nwhen she worked there.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_018: She worked in the temple? What's her name?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_019: Oh, it's Estie. But she quit the temple when she\nsettled down in Ribeira.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_020: Estie... Whoa, hang on! Nightblossom Estie?!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_021: She was a vulkan! She was a minor celestial general\nwho could command any and all kinds of magic!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_022: She fought shoulder to shoulder with Windstorm\nCastor! She's famous for it!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_023: What?! I knew mom and Castor were friends\nback then.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_024: But I can't imagine any of that. Mom? A vulkan?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_025: I don't know how you can say that. She's an\nincredibly gifted person.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_026: She's my mom, and I hardly know anything about\nher. And Tialla's a mystery to me too.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_027: Oh, come on. You're moping again. You'll make\namends. Keep your chin up!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_028: You're right, Ultand. I'll give it my best shot.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_029: I'm rootin' for ya!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_030: Nightblossom Estie is Peter's mother...
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_B_031: I've read about her in the temple records, but what\nkind of person is she?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_001: Hey, Ultand. Got any more temple stories?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_002: Sure. Since you and I started talking, I've been doing\nsome research again.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_003: How do I put it? You and Cai really are as close\nas family.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_004: You're right, but how do you get that from the\ntemple records?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_005: Well... All the records about Castor and Aurora are\nblacked out. No one can read them.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_006: So I asked Centurio. I'll tell you what he told me.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_007: Aurora was brought back to the temple shortly after\nCai was born.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_008: Castor held Cai, sobbing.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_009: That surprised Centurio. He said he'd never seen\nCastor in tears before.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_010: I'm pretty sure that's when Castor asked Estie for\nhelp in Ribeira.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_011: Estie apparently knew about Castor and Aurora and\nhad always wished them well.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_012: Whoa! Mom knew about them?!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_013: She was a strong person with a lot of integrity. She\nkept quiet about it in the temple. 
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_014: In the temple and in the village, for Castor's sake.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_015: And for Aurora too. I think she cared deeply for her.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_016: That's right. I also heard about when Estie left\nthe temple.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_017: When she headed for Ribeira, she was pregnant\nwith you, Peter.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_018: Apparently she was very happy about having a child.\nAll the priests gave her their blessings.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_019: The way you talk about her, you make it sound like\nshe's an amazing person.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_020: That's what I've been trying to tell you! She was a\nfirst-rate vulkan!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_021: I see. I'm feeling kinda proud of her.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_022: My whole life, I thought only Cai and Tialla had\nfamilies that, you know, really stood out.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_023: But that changes today 'cause my mom's awesome!
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_024: She's strong and kind and brave. I hope I can be like\nher someday.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_025: Hehehe. I like your newfound confidence, Peter. And\nI'm sure you'll become a good man.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_026: You really think so?
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_027: Yes. Give it another five years or so.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_028: Oh. That's a long time from now. Figures.
MID_SE_Pet_Hur_A_029: Don't let that get you down. Look forward to\nbecoming the man you want to be!